Subject: Cantor Phase3 Topology Scanner Formation Consistency Evidence Reconciliation Justification

& [JustificationIdentity] is exact
  + [justification_uuid] is 1bfecbc3-40bb-4445-8e12-36f957fd4dec
  + [source_snapshot_uuid] is f761e445-9961-4a1f-9adc-f973514fd542
  + [protocol_uuid] is fea5d73e-aed1-4d3c-806f-23321057610c
  + [state] is justified_unsigned

& [Need] is an inspectable current formation graph
  + current machine and receipt forms reject quiescent_double_inventory and consistency
  + preserved scanner formation still publishes those exact terms
  + a child representation revision cannot silently rewrite parent formation authority
  + no scanner runtime exists, so correction before implementation is cheaper and safer than migration afterward

& [WhyExplicitSupersession] is mandatory
  + editing preserved source or canonical formation would destroy source identity and signature meaning
  + relying on documentation alone would leave contradictory machine and formation vocabularies
  + an artifact-bound replacement formation signature records changed and inherited clauses prospectively
  + no implementation signature exists to supersede or activate

& [WhyDualAcquisitionLineage] is necessary
  + non_atomic_repeated_inventory_equal semantically requires two actual complete acquisitions
  + pure carrier equality cannot establish physical origin, distinct occurrence, completeness, or causal order
  + two independent lineages prevent one event or mutable carrier from occupying both roles
  + exact common scope prevents equality across incomparable subjects or policies
  + current reconciliation supplies only the required canonical equality edge

& [WhyAbstractCausalOrder] is sufficient at formation stage
  + first-complete-before-second-start states the required semantic relation exactly
  + choosing ticks, clock domain, API, and runtime representation is an M2C design decision
  + premature clock design would widen source beyond formation reconciliation
  + later implementation must prove the relation under separately signed authority

& [WhyScannerProfileRemains] is bounded
  + scanner profile 0.1 identifies unchanged no-follow observation and traversal policy
  + forms and receipt 0.3 identify current machine representation
  + no scanner executable exists whose backward compatibility is promised
  + any later behavior change requires new source and profile decision

& [WhyRoleSeparation] is security relevant
  + pure form validity cannot prove observation
  + evidence derivation cannot prove issuer authority
  + issuance cannot prove freshness or single use at consumption
  + separating these stages blocks caller-created receipts from becoming self-authorizing capability tokens

& [AlternativesRejected] are complete
  + proceed to M2C rejected because formation is stale and unsigned for implementation
  + implicit inheritance rejected because authority mutation becomes invisible
  + in-place edit rejected because source preservation fails
  + full scanner redesign rejected because observation behavior is not in dispute
  + runtime acquisition schema rejected because M2C is not selected
  + physical fixture rejected because M2D execution is not authorized

& [RiskReduction] is measurable
  + eliminates current vocabulary contradiction before code
  + makes every evidence conjunct and missing authority visible
  + prevents supplied equality, operand position, valid forms, or historical signatures from laundering provenance
  + preserves zero production, dependency, runtime, and physical delta

& [Cost] is bounded
  + repository governance artifacts, hashes, recursive evidence maintenance, and one replacement formation signature
  + zero production code, Cargo, API, dependency, fixture, migration, or external state
  + rollback invalidates only the replacement formation generation

& [Decision] is justified
  + complete current formation authority before any M2C source selection
  + retain every inherited scanner obligation
  + grant no implementation, execution, physical, issuer, consumer, or effect authority
